## What I built
Ported all **4 hooks** from `web/src/api/hooks/useSharing.ts` to UI-free KMP shared-core state holders, following the established S7/S8 architecture (mirroring the Push/SavedViews/Annotations ports):

**Reads (2):**
- `useShareLinks(driveId)` ΓåÆ `SharingStore.shareLinks` ΓÇö `GET /drives/{driveId}/shares`, staleTime 0, `List<ShareToken>`
- `useSharedDrive(token)` ΓåÆ `SharingStore.sharedDrive` ΓÇö public `GET /share/{token}`, staleTime SLOW(5m), `SharedDrive` union

**Mutations (2):**
- `useCreateShareLink` ΓåÆ `POST /drives/{driveId}/share`, invalidates **only** `sharingKeys.shares(driveId)`
- `useRevokeShareLink` ΓåÆ `DELETE /shares/{token}`, delete-by-token / invalidate-by-drive

**Key parity decisions:** SI preserved on the canonical `SharedDriveData` (`distance_m`/`duration_s`/`*_mps`); the legacy `SharedDriveDataV1` (`*_km`/`*_kmh`) is kept verbatim only for the share-link transition; union discriminated by `payload_version` presence via `SharedDriveSerializer`. Cache keys are prefixed so the two reads never collide in one partition.

